The user is asking for the full name of each maker, their ID, and the number of models they produce. So, I need to select the "FullName" from "car_makers", the "Id" from "car_makers", and the count of "ModelId" from "model_list".

I should use a SELECT statement. The first part will be "SELECT FullName FROM car_makers". Then, I need to get the "Id" from "car_makers", so I'll add "FROM car_makers" and "ID" in the query. For the count, I can use COUNT("ModelId") from "model_list", so I'll include that.

Putting it all together, the query should select FullName, Id, and the count of ModelIds. I should make sure the syntax is correct, using the appropriate table aliases and ensuring the SELECT statement is properly formatted.

